# Line-ending and binary policy.
#
# Suggested by @andrew-hoffman on issue #3. Two problems it solves here:
#
#   1. This repo's deployment scripts (tools/*.sh, vxd-patches/deploy_premonolith.sh) are
#      LF only by accident. With core.autocrlf=true and no rules, a fresh clone on Windows
#      hands you CRLF copies that bash refuses to run. Latent bug for anyone cloning.
#   2. This project's whole value is byte-exact binary patches. Git currently classifies
#      them correctly by autodetection alone - which works until a patched VxD happens to
#      carry no NUL byte early enough to trip the heuristic. Then it gets silently mangled.
#      The rules below make that impossible rather than unlikely.
#
# NOTE: 86box_full/ has its own .gitattributes, shipped by upstream 86Box, and a
# subdirectory's rules win. The vendored emulator tree is deliberately left under
# upstream's policy so our tree stays diffable against 86Box master.

# Default: normalise text to LF in the database, native on checkout.
* text=auto


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binaries - never convert, never diff as text
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The patched drivers and the stock originals they are derived from. The crown jewels.
*.VXD  binary
*.DRV  binary
*.SYS  binary
*.PDR  binary
*.386  binary
*.COM  binary
*.EXE  binary
*.DLL  binary
*.OVL  binary
*.CPI  binary
*.FNT  binary

# Dumps, ROM images and disk images
*.bin  binary
*.rom  binary
*.img  binary
*.dsk  binary
*.iso  binary
*.vhd  binary
*.cab  binary

# The whole ROM tree - it holds a dozen vendor-specific BIOS extensions
# (.bio .vbi .bi1 .bi2 .bi3 .awd .ami .rcv .usf .v3 .001 .004 ...) and listing
# each one is a losing game. Nothing under here is ever text.
# Use -text rather than the `binary` macro so the *.md / *.txt rules at the
# bottom of this file can still win for the handful of READMEs living in there.
roms/**        -text
test-images/** -text

# Build output and archives
*.o    binary
*.obj  binary
*.a    binary
*.lib  binary
*.pdb  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.7z   binary

# Media
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.bmp  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.pdf  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.mp4  binary


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CRLF - files consumed by DOS, Windows 3.x/9x, or a period toolchain
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Run on the real 5160 from AUTOEXEC.BAT / CONFIG.SYS. DOS is unforgiving here.
*.BAT  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.CFG  text eol=crlf
*.cfg  text eol=crlf
*.INI  text eol=crlf
*.ini  text eol=crlf
*.INF  text eol=crlf
*.inf  text eol=crlf
*.REG  text eol=crlf
*.reg  text eol=crlf

# The 1995 DDK MASM/LINK toolchain - custom_vkd/ and ivt68fix/ are assembled by
# the genuine period tools, which expect CRLF.
*.ASM  text eol=crlf
*.asm  text eol=crlf
*.INC  text eol=crlf
*.inc  text eol=crlf
*.DEF  text eol=crlf
*.def  text eol=crlf
*.map  text eol=crlf
MAKEFILE text eol=crlf

# PowerShell
*.ps1  text eol=crlf


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LF - anything executed by bash/MSYS or a modern interpreter
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
.gitignore     text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation - LF in the database, native on checkout
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

*.md   text
*.txt  text
